es for Service Mapping","description":"An entry point is a point where clients access a service instance. Service Mapping starts the mapping process for every application service from the entry point you define for it. Service Mapping includes a wide range of preconfigured entry point types that cover most commonly used applications. If your organization uses a less known or proprietary application that does not have a corresponding entry point type in Service Mapping, you must create it.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/it-operations-management/discovery-and-service-mapping-patterns/t\\_CreateEntryPoint.html","release":"australia","product":"Discovery and Service Mapping Patterns","classification":"discovery-and-service-mapping-patterns","topic_type":"task","last_updated":"2026-03-12","reading_time_minutes":3,"breadcrumb":["Discovery patterns used by ITOM Visibility","ITOM Visibility","IT Operations Management"],"tags":["#it-operations-management","#patterns","#discovery","#service-mapping","#ci","#type-task"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"key":"ServiceNowOfficialDocs/it-operations-management/discovery-and-service-mapping-patterns/t_CreateEntryPoint.md"},"smart_blocks:ServiceNowOfficialDocs/it-operations-management/discovery-and-service-mapping-patterns/t_CreateEntryPoint.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"last_embed":{"hash":"a2qmgk","at":1784578461942},"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.03575798,-0.03867782,0.00092081,-0.08487442,-0.06109414,0.01891599,0.05032323,-0.03588496,0.02196776,-0.0096383,0.02088852,-0.03157885,0.02896244,0.03640764,-0.0150131,-0.02835958,-0.040295,0.02816081,0.03088186,0.08928338,0.11573149,-0.01007903,-0.08088065,0.00251088,0.03239174,0.06265749,0.00972699,-0.00611115,0.01582406,-0.16251463,-0.0111255,0.00581315,-0.00073052,0.01224722,-0.05173807,-0.04345567,-0.02963591,0.07418929,-0.01668952,0.00228496,0.07071716,-0.04387291,-0.0238391,-0.00304349,-0.07158133,-0.0